          "dense_rank": 1,
          "lexical_score": 18.835613,
          "lexical_rank": 1,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Updating your insurance\n\nIf your insurance has changed since your last visit, tell the front desk at check-in and fill in Form IC-2, the Insurance Update Form, so the claim goes to the right plan. A new card can take up to two business days to verify. If you give us the new details at least two business days before your appointment, we can confirm your coverage before you arrive.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 605,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3325207,
          "dense_rank": 2,
          "lexical_score": 8.861862,
          "lexical_rank": 2,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact and insurance information;\n- Form PR-4, Medical History Questionnaire: your past illnesses, operations, current medicines and allergies;\n- Form HC-9, Consent to Treatment.\n\nYou can fill them in on the tablet at the self-check-in kiosk, or on paper at the front desk. Most people take about 10 minutes over them. Returning patients update Form PR-1 only when their details have changed, and complete Form PR-4 again once a year.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 591,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.32999444,
          "dense_rank": 3,
          "lexical_score": 5.3722844,
          "lexical_rank": 7,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 599,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.32948285,
          "dense_rank": 4,
          "lexical_score": 5.6751404,
          "lexical_rank": 5,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n\nThis guide lists, plan by plan, the health insurance plans we are in-network with. Insurance companies sell many plans under one brand name, and being in-network with a company does not mean being in-network with every plan it sells. Check the plan name printed on the front of your insurance card - it usually appears next to the company logo or under \"Plan\" - and compare it with the lists below.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 602,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.31805837,
          "dense_rank": 5,
          "lexical_score": 3.4343185,
          "lexical_rank": 18,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Vaccinations\n## After your vaccination\n\nPlease stay in the waiting area for 15 minutes after any vaccination, so staff can help if you feel faint or have an allergic reaction. A sore arm for a day or two is common. Bring your vaccination record to the appointment so the new dose can be added to it.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 596,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.29522413,
          "dense_rank": 6,
          "lexical_score": 3.739929,
          "lexical_rank": 14,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: When is payment due, and what payment methods do you accept?\nAnswer: Payment is due at the time of service. We accept cash, major credit and debit cards (Visa, Mastercard, American Express),",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 599,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.28686887,
          "dense_rank": 7,
          "lexical_score": 4.951956,
          "lexical_rank": 9,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Blue Cross Blue Shield\n\nWe are in-network with Blue Cross Blue Shield PPO plans, including BlueCard PPO members whose plan was issued in another state; look for the suitcase ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 604,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.28276226,
          "dense_rank": 8,
          "lexical_score": 5.1599298,
          "lexical_rank": 8,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 594,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27876723,
          "dense_rank": 9,
          "lexical_score": 2.4181914,
          "lexical_rank": 23,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insu",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 599,
          "chunk_index": 6,
          "similarity_score": 0.27647465,
          "dense_rank": 10,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Copays and deductibles\n\nYour plan decides how much you pay at the visit. A copay is a fixed amount your plan sets for each visit, and it is collected when you check in. If yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 593,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.27493715,
          "dense_rank": 11,
          "lexical_score": 2.3480198,
          "lexical_rank": 24,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Which health insurance plans do you accept?\nAnswer: We accept most major insurance providers, including Blue Cross Blue Shield, Aetna, Cigna, UnitedHealthcare, and Medicare. If you're unsure",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 603,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.27309814,
          "dense_rank": 12,
          "lexical_score": 6.527365,
          "lexical_rank": 3,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n## If the clinic is running late\n\nSometimes an earlier appointment takes longer than planned. If your practitioner is running more than 20 minutes behind, the front desk will tell you when you check in, and you can choose to wait or to pick a new time. When we know about a delay of more than 30 minutes before you leave home, we send you a text message instead.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 605,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.26624298,
          "dense_rank": 13,
          "lexical_score": 3.1453815,
          "lexical_rank": 20,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## The self-check-in kiosk\n\nReturning patients can check in at the kiosk beside the front desk instead of queuing. Scan the QR code from your 48-hour reminder text, or ty",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 599,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.26365513,
          "dense_rank": 14,
          "lexical_score": 5.5314713,
          "lexical_rank": 6,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Cigna\n\nWe are in-network with Cigna Open Access Plus (OAP) and Cigna PPO plans. Cigna LocalPlus plans are in-network only for members who live in our county; the network area",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 600,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.25807446,
          "dense_rank": 15,
          "lexical_score": 3.309215,
          "lexical_rank": 19,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Dental care guide\n## After a filling\n\nYour mouth may stay numb for two to four hours. Do not eat or drink anything hot until the numbness wears off, so you do not burn or bite yourself without notic",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 603,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.25614452,
          "dense_rank": 16,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n## Checking in on time\n\nCheck in at the front desk or at the self-check-in kiosk as soon as you arrive. Your arrival is recorded when you check in, not when you enter the building.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 598,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.25442654,
          "dense_rank": 17,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How early should I arrive before my scheduled appointment time?\nAnswer: If it is your first visit to our clinic, please arrive 15 minutes before your appointment time to complete your regist",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 604,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.25353742,
          "dense_rank": 18,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Text message reminders\n\nWe send a reminder by text message 48 hours before your appointment and another 2 hours before it. Our messages always c",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 601,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.25336984,
          "dense_rank": 19,
          "lexical_score": 3.6440637,
          "lexical_rank": 16,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n## Electrocardiogram (ECG)\n\nA resting 12-lead ECG records the electrical activity of your heart through ten small sticky electrodes placed on your chest, arms and l",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 608,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.25285983,
          "dense_rank": 20,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 606,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.24021894,
          "dense_rank": 21,
          "lexical_score": 4.457361,
          "lexical_rank": 11,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## How long we keep records\n\nWe keep adult medical records for 10 years after your last visit.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 603,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.22976077,
          "dense_rank": 22,
          "lexical_score": 3.105584,
          "lexical_rank": 21,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Running late\n## If you are running late\n\nCall the front desk on (212) 555-0142 as soon as you know you will be late, so we can tell the practitioner and plan around it. The phone line is answered Mo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 607,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.22945228,
          "dense_rank": 23,
          "lexical_score": null,
          "lexical_rank": null,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Annual physical examination\n\nAn annual physical is a preventive check-up for adults who feel well. It includes a review of your medical history and current medicines; yo",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 605,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.224904,
          "dense_rank": 24,
          "lexical_score": 6.321845,
          "lexical_rank": 4,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## While you wait\n\nFree guest Wi-Fi is available in the waiting area: the network is called VisitDoc-Guest, and the password is printed on the card at the front desk. Ple",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 599,
